Reading (honest about what the census can and cannot see): EVERY tower (both hailspires
included) is a valid fire candidate ~38-39k of 40k frames, and the cap is NEVER full at
FRAME START (sat=0 — _advance_fx drains expired fx at the END of fx_step). Yet 362 tracers
spawned in ~230k candidate frames (0.16%) and ZERO ice. The starvation is therefore
WITHIN-FRAME: fx_step order is _observe_enemies (spark + damage number PER HP DROP — 79,725 +
48,998 = the G6-era budget) -> _observe_fires (walks defense_list IN PLACEMENT ORDER: ballista×2,
bombard×2, hailspire×2 — the probe's own TOWER_IDS order) -> _advance_fx (drain LAST). By the
time the fires pass runs, the drop-pass has spent the 64-slot cap; the rare leftover slots go to
the FIRST towers in the list; the two hailspires (placed last) never get one -> ice spawned ZERO
times, bolts ≈ 0.9%. live_max=63 pins the mid-frame saturation the frame-start census can't see.
(Diag limitation declared: cand/sat is sampled at frame start, so intra-frame instants are
measured only indirectly — via live_max + the counters; code-read §5-args + the byte-identical
G6 attribution carry the causal claim together.)

